  "notes": "The curriculum's phases run Grade R–3, 4–6, 7–9 and 10–12; Grade R, compulsory since the 2024 BELA Act, is left out. Schools are usually primary (Grade R–7) and high (Grade 8–12). The school year runs January to December. The Schools Act makes attendance compulsory from Grade R in the year a learner turns 6, and the DBE's age-requirements notice (Notice 2433 of 1998) sets the age norm per grade at the grade number plus 6, so Grade 1 is 7."
